I have a complete picture. Here is my thorough report.

# Owner Registration — Complete Code Map

## Summary of key finding
The acceptance test expects the default `registrationDate` to roll off weekends (and pinned holidays) to the next business day, but **no such logic exists in the main code** — `BuildOwner` just assigns `LocalDate.now()` raw. There is a `toBusinessDay(...)` helper and a `HOLIDAYS` set in the test base, but nothing in `src/main` references `DayOfWeek`, `plusDays`, `SATURDAY`, `SUNDAY`, or holidays (grep returns nothing).

---

## 1. registrationDate — where it is set and used

Dates are represented as `java.time.LocalDate` throughout (entity column `registration_date`, JSON serialized as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`).

### Entity field — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`
```java
@Column(name = "registration_date")
private LocalDate registrationDate;

public LocalDate getRegistrationDate() { return this.registrationDate; }
public void setRegistrationDate(LocalDate registrationDate) { this.registrationDate = registrationDate; }
```

### Default server date is assigned here — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`
```java
Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);
// Default an unsupplied registration date to the server's current date.
if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
    owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
}
```
This is the ONLY place the default date comes from: a bare `LocalDate.now()` (system default zone), no weekend/holiday adjustment. The input value flows in via `OwnerMapper.toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (MapStruct; `registrationDate` is an `OwnerFields` property mapped by name, not ignored).

### OpenAPI contract — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (lines 2040-2045)
```yaml
registrationDate:
  title: Registration date
  description: The date the owner was registered. Defaults to the server's current date when not supplied. Returned in ISO 'YYYY-MM-DD' format.
  type: string
  format: date
```
`OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` are generated from this spec (no hand-written DTO files exist under `rest/dto`).

---

## 2. Membership number logic (and the year segment)

Derived, not persisted — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (lines 159-162):
```java
@Transient
public String getMembershipNumber() {
    return this.customerCode + "-M" + String.format("%02d", this.registrationDate.getYear() % 100);
}
```
The "year segment" = `-M` + last two digits (`year % 100`, zero-padded) of `registrationDate.getYear()`. Example `LON-SMI-0007-M26`. Note: it calls `registrationDate.getYear()` with no null guard, so it depends on the date default in `BuildOwner` having run.

`customerCode` prefix is built in `BuildOwner.nextCustomerCode(...)` as `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` where `NNNN` = (owners already in that city, case-insensitive) + 1:
```java
String city3 = city.substring(0, Math.min(3, city.length())).toUpperCase();
String last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();
int sequence = countOwnersInCity(city, ownerRepository) + 1;
return String.format("%s-%s-%04d", city3, last3, sequence);
```

Related derived getters in the same Owner class: `getMembershipTier()` (SILVER if `namesakeCount==0` and email present, else BRONZE), `getLocality()` (fixed CITY_REGION map Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD, else UNKNOWN), `getDisplayName()`, `getInitials()`. `namesakeCount` is computed in `BuildOwner` via `countNamesakes(...)` (case-insensitive first+last match over `findAll()`), fixed at creation.

---

## 3. Daily create-limit logic

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateDailyOwnerLimit.java`
```java
public class ValidateDailyOwnerLimit {
    private static final int DAILY_LIMIT = 100;

    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws DailyOwnerLimitException {
        LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();
        int count = 0;
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate())) {
                count++;
            }
        }
        if (count >= DAILY_LIMIT) {
            throw new DailyOwnerLimitException(
                    DAILY_LIMIT + " or more owners have already been created today");
        }
    }
}
```
Counts every owner from `ownerRepository.findAll()` whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; at ≥100 it escalates. Read-only gate, publishes nothing. Counting uses the raw `LocalDate.now()` (same bare "today" as BuildOwner) — if a business-day roll were added to the default date, this comparison would need to match it.

### Exception + handler (429)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyOwnerLimitException.java` — `extends Exception`, single-String constructor.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler.java`
```java
public void handle(@Parameter DailyOwnerLimitException ex,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<Void>> response) {
    response.send(new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS));
}
```

Analogous capacity gate (for comparison) — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateCityCapacity.java`, limit 50 per city, throws `CityAtCapacityException` (409).

---

## 4. OfficeFloor YAML — POST owners pipeline

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
Step order (each `next:` chains to the following):
1. `validate` → `ValidateNewOwner`
2. `uniqueTelephone` → `ValidateUniqueTelephone`
3. `uniqueHousehold` → `ValidateUniqueHousehold`
4. `cityCapacity` → `ValidateCityCapacity`
5. `dailyLimit` → `ValidateDailyOwnerLimit`  (comment: "Reject a create once 100 or more owners have already been created today (by registrationDate) with a 429")
6. `applyHousehold` → `ApplySharedHousehold` (govern: transaction)
7. `build` → `BuildOwner` (govern: transaction)  ← where registrationDate default + customerCode + namesakeCount are set
8. `save` → `SaveOwner` (govern: transaction)
9. `respond` → `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (govern: transaction)

Top of file: `composition.authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"`. The full contents were read; validation/uniqueness gates (steps 1-5) are read-only and run before any entity is built, and all mutation steps (6-9) are governed by `transaction`.

### Escalation mapping — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyOwnerLimitException.yml`
```yaml
handle:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler
```
(Other escalation YAMLs in the same dir map NotFound, DuplicateTelephone, CityAtCapacity, InvalidEmail/Telephone, MissingOwnerFields, DuplicateHousehold, DataIntegrityViolation, AuthorizationDenied, MethodArgumentNotValid, generic Exception.)

---

## 5. All function step classes in owner creation
Directory: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`
- `ValidateNewOwner.java` — required-field validation (step 1)
- `ValidateUniqueTelephone.java` — 409 on duplicate normalized phone (step 2)
- `ValidateUniqueHousehold.java` — 409 household gate, publishes `Household.Id` (step 3)
- `ValidateCityCapacity.java` — 409 at 50/city (step 4)
- `ValidateDailyOwnerLimit.java` — 429 at 100/day (step 5)
- `ApplySharedHousehold.java` — back-fills household id (step 6)
- `BuildOwner.java` — sets registrationDate default, customerCode, namesakeCount, householdId (step 7)
- `SaveOwner.java` — persists (step 8)
- `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` — 201 response (step 9)

Supporting (non-step helpers used by the above): `Household.java` (household id = first 12 upper-hex of SHA-256 of normalized lastName+"\n"+address; membership set), `OwnerAddress.java` (address normalize), `OwnerEmail.java`, `OwnerTelephone.java`, `ApplyOwner.java`, `ValidateOwner.java`. (Other files in the dir — ListOwners, LoadOwner, DeleteOwner, Respond\* etc. — belong to other endpoints.)

---

## 6. Existing tests for registration date / membership / create limit

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — one test:
```java
/** business-day: the default registration date must fall on a business day (a weekend rolls
 * forward to Monday)... the default registrationDate is never a Saturday or Sunday. */
@Test
void coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay() throws Exception {
    int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
    DayOfWeek dow = LocalDate.parse(fetchOwner(id).get("registrationDate").asText()).getDayOfWeek();
    assertTrue(dow != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && dow != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY, dow.toString());
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — black-box base (POST /api/owners, read back via GET). Relevant helpers:
- `today()` → `LocalDate.now().toString()`
- `createMany(int n)` — creates n owners "all dated today" to drive the per-day limit/bulk-signup rules
- `fillCity(city, n)` — drives per-city capacity
- **`toBusinessDay(LocalDate d)`** (lines 267-274) — the only business-day logic present anywhere; rolls forward over Sat/Sun and `HOLIDAYS` to next business day
- **`HOLIDAYS`** set (lines 240-242): 2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28
- Pinned reference maps `CITY_REGION`, `REGION_TIMEZONE`, `REGION_POSTCODES`
- `sha256hex`, `shaHex(s,n)`, `luhn(s)` helpers (for household id / customer-code-style assertions)
- Isolation via `@Transactional` + `@WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN, VET_ADMIN, ADMIN)`

### Weekend / business-day logic status
- Present ONLY in test base: `AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay(...)` + `HOLIDAYS`.
- Absent from main: grep for `DayOfWeek|plusDays|SATURDAY|SUNDAY|HOLIDAY|businessDay|isWeekend` across `src/main/java` returns nothing. `BuildOwner` assigns a plain `LocalDate.now()`. So the `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` test passes only on weekdays and will fail when the server date is a Saturday/Sunday (or pinned holiday) — this is the implementation gap to close, and any fix must keep `ValidateDailyOwnerLimit`'s `today` comparison consistent with whatever default date `BuildOwner` writes.

